    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file that extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Textract service. Amazon Textract is a service that automatically extracts text and data from scanned documents. I will use the Boto3 library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with the Textract service. The provider will be identifiable by the import of the Boto3 library and the use of the Textract client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789886923469,
          "start": 1789886920891
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd92f8bb001eThgreSHe4FSaY",
